2. Existing application stability and data preservation.
3. Security, privacy, and access control.
4. Patient and clinical data integrity.
5. Correct business logic and financial calculations.
6. Reliable backup and recovery.
7. Maintainable, modular architecture.
8. Developer feature management.
9. Subscription package readiness.
10. Fast performance and responsive design.
11. Professional and user-friendly experience.
12. Future scalability and maintainability.

# FINAL PRINCIPLE

Build this system as a long-term, extensible Dental Clinic Management product rather than a one-time project.

The client must be able to request new features, bug fixes, modifications, and integrations in the future.

The Developer must be able to implement, test, enable, disable, maintain, and manage those features without rebuilding the entire application or risking existing patient and clinic data.

The Developer must retain comprehensive control over global feature availability and future subscription package configuration.

Global feature toggles, subscription package entitlements, and user-role permissions must remain independent and work together through centralized authorization.

Every future feature, database migration, bug fix, and system update must integrate safely into the existing application.

The application must remain fast, responsive, secure, reliable, user-friendly, professionally designed, and maintainable.

**MOST IMPORTANT: Patient records are critical clinical information. Never sacrifice existing patient data, clinical history, uploaded documents, or database integrity for new features, convenience, speed of development, or future flexibility. Never perform risky operations without a verified backup and recovery strategy. If data safety cannot be established, stop the operation and explain the risk.**

**The ultimate goal is a professional, production-ready Dental Clinic Management System that can evolve over many years while preserving the integrity, privacy, and availability of every existing patient record.**